Class: NRM
Halflife: 1600.0 years
Shielding: Stl05 Stl30
Description: Ra226 is a naturally occuring radioactive material normally found in rocks.  At one time, it was used in radium dial watches and other "glow in the dark" devices, but is now considered too hazardous for such applications.  It is normally recognized by (and reported with) its daughter isotopes, which include radon gas.
